ignificant entity in the historical record. Relevant to cause-and-effect analysis.", "newValue": "The National Library of Korea, established in 1945 in Seoul, serves as a vital cultural institution and repository of knowledge for South Korea. It was founded in the wake of Korea's liberation from Japanese colonial rule, marking a significant pivot in the country's cultural and intellectual landscape. The library's establishment was a crucial moment in the post-war era, as it sought to preserve the rich heritage of Korean literature, history, and culture while promoting national identity during a time of reconstruction and modernization.

